1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:02,336
The world worships the rising sun.

2
00:00:02,336 --> 00:00:05,004
Chhath honors the setting sun too. Why?

3
00:00:05,004 --> 00:00:07,330
Earlier, the sun fed Yudhishthira.

4
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:10,800
But the setting sun's secret hides in two texts.

5
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:12,340
First clue: the Vedas.

6
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:14,533
The Taittiriya Aranyaka says,

7
00:00:14,533 --> 00:00:16,678
every evening as the sun sets,

8
00:00:16,678 --> 00:00:19,180
Demons named Mandeh attack the sun.

9
00:00:20,180 --> 00:00:23,790
Then sages chant the Gayatri and toss water toward the sun.

10
00:00:23,790 --> 00:00:25,686
That water turns into a weapon,

11
00:00:25,686 --> 00:00:26,910
and the demons flee.

12
00:00:27,410 --> 00:00:29,526
Meaning arghya is not just prayer,

13
00:00:29,526 --> 00:00:31,082
it is defense of the sun.

14
00:00:31,082 --> 00:00:33,135
But the Veda does not stop there.

15
00:00:33,135 --> 00:00:34,380
It is written there:

16
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:39,446
Whoever meditates on both the rising and setting sun attains all auspiciousness.

17
00:00:39,446 --> 00:00:42,290
And the same truth was heard again amid a war.

18
00:00:42,710 --> 00:00:45,608
The second clue is in the Valmiki Ramayana...

19
00:00:45,608 --> 00:00:47,540
The Lanka war... Ravana ahead.

20
00:00:47,650 --> 00:00:49,757
And Rama, tired from fighting,

21
00:00:49,757 --> 00:00:51,232
was drowned in worry.

22
00:00:51,232 --> 00:00:53,480
Then Sage Agastya came and said:

23
00:00:53,710 --> 00:00:54,586
[Agastya] Rama,

24
00:00:54,586 --> 00:00:56,337
listen to this Aditya Hridaya.

25
00:00:56,337 --> 00:00:57,329
By chanting this,

26
00:00:57,329 --> 00:00:59,430
you will conquer every enemy in war.

27
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:00,230
In that hymn,

28
00:01:00,230 --> 00:01:03,520
there is a verse that reveals the whole secret of Chhath:

29
00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:05,357
[Sanskrit] Namah purvaya giraye,

30
00:01:05,357 --> 00:01:06,490
pashchimayadraye namah.

31
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:09,829
Salutations to the rising sun on the eastern mountain,

32
00:01:09,829 --> 00:01:12,000
and to the setting sun on the west.

33
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:14,761
Rama gazed at the sun, chanted thrice,

34
00:01:14,761 --> 00:01:17,610
and his worry vanished. Then Ravana fell.

35
00:01:17,610 --> 00:01:19,070
You have your answer.

36
00:01:19,270 --> 00:01:24,700
Both the Vedas and the Ramayana give the setting sun as much reverence as the rising one.

37
00:01:26,110 --> 00:01:27,502
Chhath isn't named here,

38
00:01:27,502 --> 00:01:29,300
but this tradition starts here.

39
00:01:29,410 --> 00:01:33,778
That is why Chhath offers arghya to both the setting and rising suns.

40
00:01:33,778 --> 00:01:36,120
But the real message is what follows.

41
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:38,170
We all salute good days.

42
00:01:39,830 --> 00:01:43,184
But when the day starts to fade and things slip from our hands,

43
00:01:43,184 --> 00:01:44,249
the mind turns away.

44
00:01:44,249 --> 00:01:45,900
Chhath does the exact opposite.

45
00:01:46,020 --> 00:01:46,688
In Chhath,

46
00:01:46,688 --> 00:01:49,830
devotees first offer arghya to the setting sun,

47
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:52,836
Then wait through the night, and at dawn,

48
00:01:52,836 --> 00:01:54,020
to the rising sun.

49
00:01:54,020 --> 00:01:55,730
Meaning Chhath teaches us:

50
00:01:55,850 --> 00:01:57,778
A fading day is not defeat,

51
00:01:57,778 --> 00:01:59,564
but a promise of morning.

52
00:01:59,564 --> 00:02:01,063
Bow to your bad days.

53
00:02:01,063 --> 00:02:02,920
They lead you to the dawn.

54
00:02:03,020 --> 00:02:05,924
Try doing this today: This evening as the sun sets,

55
00:02:05,924 --> 00:02:08,030
pause for a minute and thank the day.

56
00:02:09,950 --> 00:02:11,044
No matter the day.

57
00:02:11,044 --> 00:02:13,110
The world worships the rising sun,

58
00:02:13,110 --> 00:02:15,480
but morning comes from the setting one.

59
00:02:16,050 --> 00:02:18,180
Share this story with your loved ones.

60
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:20,814
Maybe it will help someone whose day is fading.

61
00:02:20,814 --> 00:02:21,430
Next story:

62
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:22,926
Arjuna was trembling,

63
00:02:22,926 --> 00:02:24,840
and Krishna was smiling. Why?

